    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Notes\n\n- All wiring and electrical connections should comply with the National Electrical Code (NEC) and with local codes and practices.\n- **Apparent Power**: The power supplied to the electric circuit - typical from a power supplier to the grid - to cover the real and reactive power consumption in the loads.\n- **For rows marked 'See note'**: The local power company should be consulted.\n- If undersized wire is used between the motor and the power source, the starting and load carrying capabilities of the motor will be limited.\n\n## Conversion Factors\n\n- 1 hp = 0.746 kW\n- 1 ft (foot) = 0.3048 m\n\n## Wire Gauge (AWG) Reference\n\nThe table above provides recommended copper wire gauges (American Wire Gauge) based on motor horsepower, operating voltage (230V or 460V three-phase), apparent power in kVA, and distance from motor to transformer in feet. Lower AWG numbers indicate larger diameter wires."
